## 4. Noncommercial Purposes

Any noncommercial purpose is permitted. A noncommercial purpose is any purpose that is not a commercial purpose.

A commercial purpose is any purpose of using, or directing work to use, the software or any part of it, with or without changes:

(a) for commercial advantage,

(b) for monetary compensation, or

(c) in connection with any revenue-generating product, service, or business activity.

Examples of commercial purposes include:

(1) charging users, customers, or clients to access, run, or use the software;

(2) providing paid consulting, hosting, deployment, managed infrastructure, or support services for the software;

(3) incorporating the software, in whole or in part, into any proprietary commercial product, platform, or service;

(4) using the software internally within any for-profit commercial entity, enterprise, or business to support its operations, infrastructure, or commercial revenue generation.

Noncommercial purposes include personal study, research, education, individual edge IoT experimentation, testing, and non-monetized hobbyist use.

